d-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062085/state.json" "file_sha256" "85a68e41755b99591fd81bb18a2bc8610a0a1447bbb6747262ca07e0cc856680"} {"question" "q-317612" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we are told that $T$ represents a stretch along the $x$-axis or $y$-axis.\n\nComparing the $x$- and $y$-components of $u$ and $T(u),$ we note the following:\n\n- the $x$-components of $u$ and $T(u)$ are the same, while\n\n- the $y$-component of $T(u)$ is $\\sqrt{3}$ times the $y$-component of $u.$\n\nSo, we conclude that $T$ represents a stretch of scale factor $\\sqrt{3}$ in the $y$-direction. \n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062085/state.json" "file_sha256" "85a68e41755b99591fd81bb18a2bc8610a0a1447bbb6747262ca07e0cc856680"} {"question" "q-317612" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062085/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b71482df4e5a7ceaa2278712357f7b8769bb9dc5141cdda2dfbfcd1200ebf66d"} {"question" "q-317612" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062085/state.json" "file_sha256" "85a68e41755b99591fd81bb18a2bc8610a0a1447bbb6747262ca07e0cc856680"} {"question" "q-317612" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-c