ence/mathacademy/question-capture/14062085/assets/8674e7345c903bf193e09cc9ae1702383cad10ba06c5dc3b6d2713ea30eb843e.png)\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $T$ represents a stretch with a scale factor $3$ in the $y$-direction." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062085/state.json" "file_sha256" "85a68e41755b99591fd81bb18a2bc8610a0a1447bbb6747262ca07e0cc856680"} {"question" "q-38020" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062085/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b71482df4e5a7ceaa2278712357f7b8769bb9dc5141cdda2dfbfcd1200ebf66d"} {"question" "q-38020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062085/state.json" "file_sha256" "85a68e41755b99591fd81bb18a2bc8610a0a1447bbb6747262ca07e0cc856680"} {"question" "q-38020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "A horizontal shear with a shear factor of $3$"] ["text" "A stretch of scale factor $3$ in the $x$-direction"] ["text" "A stretch of scale factor $3$ in the $y$-direction"] ["text" "A stretch of scale factor $\\frac{1}{3}$ in the $x$-direction"] ["text" "A vertical shear with a shear factor of $3$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062085/state.json" "file_sha256" "85a68e41755b99591fd81bb18a2bc8610a0a1447bbb6747262ca07e0cc856680"} {"question" "q-38020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "A stretch of scale factor $3$ in the $y$-direction"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062085/state.json" "file_sha256" "85a68e41755b99591fd81bb18a2bc8610a0a1447bbb6747262ca07e0cc856680"} {"question" "q-81327" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the standard basis ${i,j}$ of ${R}^{2}.$ If $T$ is a linear transformation such that $T(i)=i$ and $T(j)=-i+j,$ then what is the geometric interpretation of the transformation $T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062085/state.json" "file_sha256" "85a68e41755b99591fd81bb18a2bc8610a0a1447bbb6747262ca07e0cc856680"} {"question" "q-81327" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's consider the unit square spanned by the vectors $i$ and $j.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062085/assets/db15a65fd944c24ea2545baea08e6a0789b749295f623d8d4fdc2f07a37d4b73.png)\n\nNow, using the fact that $T(i)=i$ and $T(j)=-i+j,$ we can draw the image of the square under the transformation $T:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062085/assets/cee26b17d477344e138c3d6d9228f23d67c4c78ce447b1c2c3a887b79125ee7a.png)\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $T$ represents a horizontal shear with a shear factor of $-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062085/state.json" "file_sha256" "85a68e41755b99591fd81bb18a2bc8610a0a1447bbb6747262ca07e0cc856680"} {"question" "q-81327" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062085/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b71482df4e5a7ceaa2278712357f7b8769bb9dc5141cdda2dfbfcd1200ebf66d"} {"question" "q-81327" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/q